// The executable's icon, linked into text-editor.exe by both native profiles.
//
// Ordinal 1, and it is the only icon here, because Windows shows a program's *lowest-numbered* icon resource
// wherever it shows the program itself -- Explorer, the taskbar's pinned button, a shortcut, the Apps entry.
// editor.ico is vex.svg (the suite icon canvas's Vex primary, dark) rendered at 16 to 256 px by vex-suite-common's
// tools/Ico.java; it keeps the name installer.json and the published release already use. The window, file and
// light variants are beside it. The running window does not wear it yet: that waits on a generated wiring being able
// to name an icon (docs/TODO.md).
1 ICON "editor.ico"

// The manifest: PerMonitorV2 DPI awareness and the OS compatibility java.exe declares, so this executable is
// drawn at the display's real pixels exactly as a JVM launch is, rather than rendered at 96 DPI and stretched by
// Windows. Resource 1 of type 24 (RT_MANIFEST) is the one the loader reads for a process.
1 24 "editor.manifest"
